1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:08,460
A straight-beam calibration teaches the Epoch two things: where zero really is, and how fast sound travels in the part.

2
00:00:08,460 --> 00:00:17,730
The machine only measures time. Thickness equals velocity times time, divided by two, because the sound goes down and comes back.

3
00:00:17,730 --> 00:00:26,600
Zero is the delay through the wear plate and couplant. Velocity is the speed in steel. Two unknowns, so we need two known thicknesses.

4
00:00:26,600 --> 00:00:36,680
The Epoch has just been reset. Velocity is 0.2300 inches per microsecond, the book value for steel, and zero is 0.000.

5
00:00:36,680 --> 00:00:40,840
Put couplant on the 0.200 inch step and place the probe.

6
00:00:40,840 --> 00:00:52,790
On the far left is the initial pulse. The next signal is the first back-wall echo. It sits at about 0.26 on the screen, not 0.200, because zero is not set yet.

7
00:00:52,790 --> 00:00:58,980
Press GATES, press the check key for bigger steps, and move Gate 1 over the first back-wall echo.

8
00:00:58,980 --> 00:01:06,780
Make sure the gate is on the back-wall echo, not on the initial pulse. The red marker shows which signal the gate is measuring.

9
00:01:06,780 --> 00:01:11,060
Press 2nd F, then GATES, to bring the echo to 80 percent.

10
00:01:11,060 --> 00:01:15,620
Now press F3 for Auto Cal, then P2 for Cal-Zero.

11
00:01:15,620 --> 00:01:19,910
Turn the knob to enter the known thickness: 0.200 inch.

12
00:01:19,910 --> 00:01:27,190
Press P6, Continue. Continue, not Done. The Epoch keeps this first point and waits for the second one.

13
00:01:27,190 --> 00:01:30,470
Move the probe to the 0.500 inch step.

14
00:01:30,470 --> 00:01:35,350
Press GATES and move Gate 1 onto the first back-wall echo of this step.

15
00:01:35,350 --> 00:01:38,670
Bring it to 80 percent with 2nd F and GATES.

16
00:01:38,670 --> 00:01:42,780
Press F3 for Auto Cal, then P3 for Cal-Vel.

17
00:01:42,780 --> 00:01:48,880
The value already reads 0.500. If it did not, you would turn the knob until it did.

18
00:01:48,880 --> 00:01:55,620
Press P7, Done. The Epoch now works out both the velocity and the zero from the two points.

19
00:01:55,620 --> 00:02:07,380
Velocity is now 0.2320 and zero is 0.500 microseconds. Zero is where the line starts. Velocity is its slope. Two points fix the line.

20
00:02:07,380 --> 00:02:14,480
Now verify on steps you did not calibrate on. Move to the 0.300 inch step and gate its echo.

21
00:02:14,480 --> 00:02:17,330
It reads 0.300. Good.

22
00:02:17,330 --> 00:02:20,940
Now the 0.400 inch step.

23
00:02:20,940 --> 00:02:24,710
It reads 0.400. The calibration is good.

24
00:02:24,710 --> 00:02:37,780
Why not verify on 0.200 or 0.500? They were used to build the calibration, so they read correctly by definition. 0.300 and 0.400 are independent checks.

25
00:02:37,780 --> 00:02:46,220
Common mistakes: gating the initial pulse, skipping AUTO 80 percent, and pressing Done after Cal-Zero instead of Continue.

26
00:02:46,220 --> 00:02:50,210
Now try it yourself on the Epoch below.
